function [lat, lon, alt] = geodetic_with(r, re, f)
%GEODETIC_WITH  Geodetic latitude, longitude [rad] and height of an Earth-fixed position on an ellipsoid of equatorial radius re
%   and flattening f.
%   r: real[m][3] (passed in m)
%   re: real[m] (passed in m)
%   f: real[1] (passed a plain number)
%   returns lat: real[1] (passed a plain number)
%   returns lon: real[1] (passed a plain number)
%   returns alt: real[m] (passed in m)
%   Generated by tools/pcode.py from the pseudocode (trinetra-pcode/2); do not edit.
    lat = 0;
    lon = 0;
    alt = 0;
    x = r(1);
    y = r(2);
    z = r(3);
    e2 = (f * (2 - f));
    lon = atan2(y, x);
    p = hypot(x, y);
    la = atan2(z, (p * (1 - e2)));
    for k = (0):((5) - 1)
        sph = sin(la);
        h__263 = (1 - (e2 * (sph * sph)));
        if h__263 < 0, h__263 = NaN; else, h__263 = sqrt(h__263); end
        n = (re / h__263);
        al = ((p / cos(la)) - n);
        la = atan2(z, (p * (1 - ((e2 * n) / (n + al)))));
    end
    sph2 = sin(la);
    h__264 = (1 - (e2 * (sph2 * sph2)));
    if h__264 < 0, h__264 = NaN; else, h__264 = sqrt(h__264); end
    n2 = (re / h__264);
    alt = ((p / cos(la)) - n2);
    lat = la;
end
